(https://cursor.com/marketplace/agentmail) with `/add-plugin agentmail`; Codex and Claude Code add
the repository as a marketplace and install `agentmail@agentmail` from it.

Grok Bot: AgentMail is listed in the plugin browser Grok Bot ships with, alongside the other
official plugins. Install via Settings -> Plugins -> search AgentMail -> Install, then approve the
OAuth prompt. Twenty-four email tools appear and every bot on the account can call them. Where the
plugin browser is locked down, add AgentMail as a custom MCP connector at
https://mcp.agentmail.to/mcp with an `x-api-key: YOUR_API_KEY` header. The same MCP server serves
Grok Build via `grok mcp add` and the Grok API. AgentMail is an independent company; the
marketplace listing is the extent of the xAI relationship.

## OpenClaw Plugin (Official)

AgentMail is an official plugin on ClawHub, the OpenClaw plugin registry, published under the
`@agentmail` account. ClawHub lists twenty-five channel plugins for OpenClaw and every other one
is a chat surface (WhatsApp, Matrix, Discord, Slack, Teams, Feishu, LINE, Google Chat, QQ, Zalo,
Nostr, Twitch, Urbit, iMessage via BlueBubbles). AgentMail is the email one.

Install:
```
openclaw plugins install clawhub:@agentmail/agentmail
openclaw plugins enable agentmail
```

The plugin ships two capabilities:

1. **CLI-backed AgentMail skill.** The agent drives the official AgentMail CLI bundled with the
   plugin and reads its help output at runtime, so new API resources work without a plugin
   release. Covers inboxes, messages, threads, drafts, webhooks, domains, pods, and API keys.
   Passthrough command: `openclaw agentmail -- --format json inboxes list`
2. **Email channel.** A durable, allowlisted, reply-only channel. Inbound email drives an agent
   turn and the agent replies inside the AgentMail thread. Ingress is committed durably before
   acknowledgement, senders are authorized against a default-deny allowlist, and replies stay
   bound to the triggering message (no proactive threads, no arbitrary recipients).

Configuration:
- `AGENTMAIL_API_KEY` in the Gateway environment (`~/.openclaw/.env` for a managed Gateway).
- `AGENTMAIL_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (optional, Svix-signed) enables webhook ingress; without it the
  channel falls back to WebSocket ingress.
- Channel settings live under `channels.agentmail` (or `channels.agentmail.accounts.<id>` for
  several inboxes): `inboxId`, `dmPolicy` (defaults to `allowlist`), `allowFrom`, `mediaMaxMb`.

Requirements: OpenClaw 2026.7.2 (beta) or newer; Node.js 22.22.3+, 24.15.0+, or 25.9.0+.
Listing: https://clawhub.ai/agentmail
Integration page: https://www.agentmail.to/build/openclaw

